    <statement><image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/ez-changing-transformations-WW4-image-1.png" width="41%"/>
<p>The figure above is the graph of the function <m>m(t)</m>.
Let <m>n(t)=m(t)+2</m>, <m>k(t)=m(t+1.5)</m>,<m>w(t)=m(t-0.5)-2.5</m> and
<m>p(t)=m(t-1)</m>. Find the values of the following:</p>
<p><alert>1.</alert> <m>n(-2.5)</m>= <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
<p><alert>2.</alert> <m>n(2)</m>= <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/>.</p>
<p><alert>3.</alert> <m>k(3)</m>= <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/>.</p>
<p><alert>4.</alert> <m>w(2.5)</m>= <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/>.</p>
<p><alert>5.</alert> <m>w(-1.5)</m>= <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/>.</p>
<p><alert>6.</alert> <m>p(2)</m>= <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>1.</alert>
Since <m>n(t)=m(t)+2</m>, we have <m>n(-2.5)=m(-2.5)+2=-3+2=-1</m>. 



<alert>2.</alert>
Since <m>n(t)=m(t)+2</m>, we have <m>n(2) =m(2)+2=6</m>.



<alert>3.</alert>
Since <m>k(t)=m(t+1.5)</m>, we have <m>k(3)=m(3+1.5)=m(4.5)=3</m>. 



<alert>4.</alert>
Since <m>w(t)=m(t-0.5)-2.5</m>, we have 
<m>w(2.5)=m(2.5-0.5)-2.5=m(2)-2.5=1.5</m>



<alert>5.</alert>
Since <m>w(t)=m(t-0.5)-2.5</m>, we have
<m>w(-1.5)=m(-1.5-0.5)-2.5=m(-2)-2.5=-5.5</m>. 



<alert>6.</alert>
Since <m>p(t)=m(t-1)</m>, we have <m>p(2)=m(2-1)=m(1)=6</m>.



</solution>
